{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yin/vm/engine_test.cljc | sed -n '243,278p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc | sed -n '266,313p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc | sed -n '100,118p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc | sed -n '157,173p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc | sed -n '104,124p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/ffi.cljc | head -5\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/dao.stream.md | sed -n '532,575p'; nl -ba docs/design/dao.await.md | sed -n '418,437p'; nl -ba docs/design/datom.world.md | sed -n '113,121p'; date -u '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S GMT'\"","aggregated_output":"   532\t## Reading\n   533\t\n   534\t`next` takes a handle and a cursor and returns an outcome immediately.\n   535\tIt is total and non-blocking: every state of the stream has a defined data\n   536\tanswer.\n   537\t\n   538\t| Outcome                       | Meaning                                                                       | Required keys                                                                           |\n   539\t|-------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n   540\t| `:dao.stream/ok`              | A value was observed.                                                         | `:dao.stream/value`, `:dao.stream/cursor` (successor)                                   |\n   541\t| `:dao.stream/blocked`         | Nothing at this position yet; retry later.                                    | —                                                                                       |\n   542\t| `:dao.stream/end`             | What this handle is on is closed and this position is past the retained tail. | —                                                                                       |\n   543\t| `:dao.stream/gap`             | This position was evicted.                                                    | `:dao.stream/cursor` (earliest retained position, or the tail when nothing is retained) |\n   544\t| `:dao.stream/cursor-mismatch` | The cursor was minted by a different logical stream.                          | —                                                                                       |\n   545\t| `:dao.stream/invalid-cursor`  | The value is not a cursor.                                                    | —                                                                                       |\n   546\t| `:dao.stream/transport-error` | The transport failed to perform the read; nothing was observed.               | —                                                                                       |\n   547\t\n   548\tReading never mutates the stream. Two readers with cursors at the same\n   549\tposition observe the same retained value; neither can starve or affect the\n   550\tother. There is no destructive read anywhere in the contract — no drain, no\n   551\ttake. An operation that removes an element as it reads would make one\n   552\treader's progress every other reader's data loss.\n   553\t\n   554\t## Writing\n   555\t\n   556\t`append!` takes a handle and a value and returns an outcome:\n   557\t\n   558\t| Outcome                       | Meaning                                                                                                                                              | Required keys |\n   559\t|-------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------|\n   560\t| `:dao.stream/ok`              | The value is accepted at the next position in the sequence this handle's writer surface is on. Implies neither local readability nor remote delivery. | —             |\n   561\t| `:dao.stream/full`            | The transport does not accept the value; nothing was appended. Whether this is transient or permanent is the transport's declared nature (see Retention and Gaps). | —             |\n   562\t| `:dao.stream/invalid-value`   | The transport cannot carry this value (for example, it cannot be encoded); nothing was appended.                                                     | —             |\n   563\t| `:dao.stream/closed`          | What this handle is on is closed to new appends; the value was not appended.                                                                         | —             |\n   564\t| `:dao.stream/transport-error` | The transport failed to perform the append; nothing was appended.                                                                                    | —             |\n   565\t\n   566\tAcceptance is handle-relative, as close outcomes are. **Which sequence** a\n   567\thandle's writer surface is on is part of the transport's declared nature: for a\n   568\tring buffer it is the logical stream itself, so `ok` places the value in it; for\n   569\ta transport that carries values toward a stream elsewhere it is the ordered\n   570\toutbound path, and what becomes of the value at the far end is reported there,\n   571\tnot here. No remote transport can say more — under *no operation waits*, an\n   572\tanswer from the far end cannot arrive before `append!` returns.\n   573\t\n   574\tThe writer decides what to do about any non-`ok` outcome; DaoStream does not\n   575\tretry, buffer, or notify on its behalf.\n   418\tIf a read is blocked or a write is full:\n   419\t\n   420\t- Yin parks the current continuation.\n   421\t- The park entry is wrapped as a `dao.runtime` task using the existing VM\n   422\t  adapter path.\n   423\t- `dao.runtime` records the task in the wait set. There are no\n   424\t  transport-local waiters: the polling wait set is the only mechanism.\n   425\t- Nothing wakes the task. Each poll resolves the entry against its transport —\n   426\t  `next` for a parked read, `append!` for a parked write — and a poll that\n   427\t  resolves it moves it to the ready queue. A stream that is written to,\n   428\t  drained, or closed wakes nothing: there are no drains, and `close!` returns\n   429\t  no wake list. A reader parked on a stream that is then closed learns of it\n   430\t  from its own next `next` answering `end`; a parked writer from `append!`\n   431\t  answering `closed`.\n   432\t- `dao.runtime` invokes the task's `:resume` function with the polled\n   433\t  outcome.\n   434\t- The VM restores the Yin continuation and continues evaluating the await body.\n   435\t\n   436\t`dao.await` must not implement these steps itself. It relies on the existing\n   437\tYin and runtime machinery.\n   113\tinterpretation. Neither is the depositor's decision.\n   114\t\n   115\tTwo things are not adapters. One that exposes a function for portable code to\n   116\tcall isolates the host library but keeps the coupling, and the effect never\n   117\tappears as an emission. One that takes a function to invoke has relocated the\n   118\tcallback, not removed it, even when every value it passes is plain data; if\n   119\tthat callback has a meaningful return value, it is a synchronous call in both\n   120\tdirections wearing the shape of an event.\n   121\t\n2026-09-19 18:09:18 GMT\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yin/vm/engine_test.cljc | sed -n '243,278p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc | sed -n '266,313p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc | sed -n '100,118p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc | sed -n '157,173p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc | sed -n '104,124p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/ffi.cljc | head -5\"","aggregated_output":"   243\t(deftest wait-set-is-resolved-from-the-store-test\n   244\t  (testing \"A parked reader is woken by polling, and its cursor advances\"\n   245\t    (let [[_ s0] (engine/handle-make (state) {:capacity 4} :stream-0)\n   246\t          [_ s1] (engine/handle-cursor s0\n   247\t                                       {:stream {:type :stream-ref,\n   248\t                                                 :id :stream-0}}\n   249\t                                       :cursor-0)\n   250\t          handle (get (:store s1) :stream-0)\n   251\t          before (get-in s1 [:store :cursor-0 :cursor])\n   252\t          parked (assoc s1\n   253\t                        :blocked? true\n   254\t                        :wait-set [{:reason :next,\n   255\t                                    :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref,\n   256\t                                                 :id :cursor-0}}])]\n   257\t      (is (= 1 (count (:wait-set (engine/check-wait-set parked))))\n   258\t          \"Nothing to read: it stays parked\")\n   259\t      (stream/append! handle :v)\n   260\t      (let [woken (engine/check-wait-set parked)\n   261\t            entry (first (:ready-queue woken))]\n   262\t        (is (empty? (:wait-set woken)))\n   263\t        (is (= :v (:value entry)))\n   264\t        (is (= {:cursor-0 {:stream-id :stream-0,\n   265\t                           :cursor (:cursor entry)}}\n   266\t               (:store-updates entry)))\n   267\t        (is (not= before (:cursor entry)))))))\n   268\t\n   269\t\n   270\t(defn- cursor-waiter\n   271\t  \"A parked reader on :cursor-0, distinguishable by its continuation.\"\n   272\t  [k]\n   273\t  {:reason :next,\n   274\t   :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id :cursor-0},\n   275\t   :k k,\n   276\t   :env {}})\n   277\t\n   278\t\n   266\t(defn- augment-wait-entry\n   267\t  \"Resolve one wait entry to a live handle and an opaque cursor out of the\n   268\t   store. The cursor is re-resolved on every round even when an earlier round\n   269\t   baked a value into the entry: another waiter on the same cursor-ref may\n   270\t   have advanced the stored cursor since.\"\n   271\t  [store entry]\n   272\t  (if-let [cursor-ref (:cursor-ref entry)]\n   273\t    (let [cursor-data (get store (:id cursor-ref))]\n   274\t      (assoc entry\n   275\t             :stream (or (:stream entry)\n   276\t                         (get store (:stream-id cursor-data)))\n   277\t             :cursor (:cursor cursor-data)))\n   278\t    (if (and (not (:stream entry)) (:stream-id entry))\n   279\t      (assoc entry :stream (get store (:stream-id entry)))\n   280\t      entry)))\n   281\t\n   282\t\n   283\t(defn- poll-wait-entry\n   284\t  \"Poll one resolved wait entry against its transport, synchronously.\n   285\t\n   286\t   Returns nil while the entry must keep waiting — `blocked` for a reader,\n   287\t   `full` for a writer, the only two outcomes that can change on their own —\n   288\t   and otherwise the ready-entry updates `{:value :status}`, plus `:cursor`\n   289\t   for a reader that moved. `end` and `gap` resolve to the values the\n   290\t   immediate path yields; any other outcome resolves under its own keyword\n   291\t   for `resume-from-run-queue` to raise. A parked writer retries by\n   292\t   appending: the append is an effect of this poll. An entry with no known\n   293\t   `:reason` keeps waiting.\"\n   294\t  [entry]\n   295\t  (case (:reason entry)\n   296\t    :next (let [result (stream/next (:stream entry) (:cursor entry))\n   297\t                o (outcome result)]\n   298\t            (case o\n   299\t              :dao.stream/ok {:value (:dao.stream/value result),\n   300\t                              :status :ok,\n   301\t                              :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor result)}\n   302\t              :dao.stream/blocked nil\n   303\t              :dao.stream/end {:value nil, :status :end}\n   304\t              :dao.stream/gap {:value :dao.stream/gap,\n   305\t                               :status :dao.stream/gap,\n   306\t                               :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor result)}\n   307\t              {:value o, :status o}))\n   308\t    :put (let [o (outcome (stream/append! (:stream entry) (:datom entry)))]\n   309\t           (case o\n   310\t             :dao.stream/ok {:value (:datom entry), :status :ok}\n   311\t             :dao.stream/full nil\n   312\t             {:value o, :status o}))\n   313\t    nil))\n   100\t         :env E\n   101\t         :k (if (seq K) K nil)\n   102\t         :halted? (and (not (:blocked? vm)) (nil? seg))))\n   103\t\n   104\t\n   105\t(defn- response-wait-entry\n   106\t  \"The polling wait entry for a sent call awaiting its correlated response:\n   107\t   the machine registers {segment pc env stack k} plus the call-out reader\n   108\t   fields, in the shape `ffi/call-response-wait-entry` gives the walker.\"\n   109\t  [seg pc env stack k call-id]\n   110\t  {:segment seg, :pc pc, :env env, :stack stack, :k k,\n   111\t   :call-id call-id,\n   112\t   :reason :next,\n   113\t   :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id vm/call-out-cursor-key},\n   114\t   :stream-id vm/call-out-stream-key})\n   115\t\n   116\t\n   117\t(defn semantic-restore\n   118\t  \"Restore a wait-set or ready-queue entry into machine registers.\n   157\t(defn- call-park-entries\n   158\t  \"Wait-entry builders for an instruction whose effect may block. The\n   159\t   continuation of an effect is the machine state after the instruction:\n   160\t   {segment, pc+1, env, stack, k} plus the transport fields the engine\n   161\t   fills in (§3.5). `St` is the operand stack with the instruction's operands\n   162\t   already popped.\"\n   163\t  [seg pc E St K]\n   164\t  {:stream/put (fn [_state _effect result]\n   165\t                 {:segment seg, :pc (inc pc), :env E, :stack St, :k K,\n   166\t                  :reason :put,\n   167\t                  :stream-id (:stream-id result)})\n   168\t   :stream/next (fn [_state _effect result]\n   169\t                  {:segment seg, :pc (inc pc), :env E, :stack St, :k K,\n   170\t                   :reason :next,\n   171\t                   :cursor-ref (:cursor-ref result),\n   172\t                   :stream-id (:stream-id result)})})\n   173\t\n   104\t  [state result k env]\n   105\t  (if (module/effect? result)\n   106\t    (let [{:keys [state value blocked?]}\n   107\t          (engine/handle-effect\n   108\t            state\n   109\t            result\n   110\t            {:restore-fn ast-walker-restore,\n   111\t             :park-entry-fns {:stream/put (fn [_s _e r]\n   112\t                                            {:k k,\n   113\t                                             :env env,\n   114\t                                             :reason :put,\n   115\t                                             :stream-id (:stream-id r),\n   116\t                                             :datom (:val result)}),\n   117\t                              :stream/next (fn [_s _e r]\n   118\t                                             {:k k,\n   119\t                                              :env env,\n   120\t                                              :reason :next,\n   121\t                                              :cursor-ref (:cursor-ref r),\n   122\t                                              :stream-id (:stream-id r)})}})]\n   123\t      (if blocked?\n   124\t        (assoc state\nnl: src/cljc/yin/repl/ffi.cljc: No such file or directory\n","exit_code":0,